<pre class=metadata>
Title: Foo
Group: test
Shortname: foo
Level: 1
Status: LS
ED: http://example.com/foo
Abstract: Testing mergeMarkup() for IDL blocks.
Editor: Example Editor
Date: 1970-01-01
</pre>

Original markup in untouched text is fine,
as is original markup fully contained or coincident with parser markup.

<pre class=idl>
// A comment with <i>italic</i> and <b>bold</b> text
interface <span class="highlight"><b>Foo</b></span> {
    attribute <mark>D</mark>OM<mark>S</mark>trin<mark>g</mark> foo;
};
</pre>

Original markup that contains parser markup is invalid,
as is original markup that would misnest with parser marker.
However, children of an invalid element might be valid.

<pre class=idl>
interface <x-bad>Bar {</x-bad>
    attribut<x-bad>e lo</x-bad>ng b<x-bad>a<mark>r</mark>;</x-bad>
};
</pre>

When an original &lt;dfn> or &lt;a> is coincident with a parser element,
drop the element, but force its dfn/link attributes onto the original.
Explicit links don't take link attributes, since they won't autolink anyway.

<pre class=idl>
interface <dfn at-rule id="legacy-id">Baz</dfn> {
    attribute <a href="http://example.com/string">DOMString</a> <a property for="Qux">baz</a>;
    attribute <a class=good>DOMString</a> baz2;
    attribute <dfn>DOMString</dfn> baz3;
};
</pre>

<dfn attribute for=Baz>baz</dfn>

Nesting an &lt;xmp> into a &lt;pre class=idl> throws a warning, but safely removes the &lt;xmp>, merging its attributes upwards.

<pre class=idl>
    <xmp class=foo other-attr="bar">
    interface Qux {
        attribute Promise<undefined> qux;
    };
    </xmp>
</pre>